th former POTUS Barrack Obama and former VP Joe Biden.  /44/2Q08/10/obamas-175000-donor.html'). Mary Biskup of Missouri appeared to give more than $170,000  in small donations to the 2008 Obama campaign. Yet Biskup said she never gave any money to the  campaign. Some other contributor gave the donations using her name, without her knowledge. (The   published in the Washington Post a story about Mary Biskup, a woman in who's  name $175,000 in contributions to the Obama Campaign during 2008 were made  (well in excess of federal limits) and later returned. Two things stand out about that   Kristen Welker is the 13th moderator of \"\"Meet the Press,\"\" the hourlong NBC Sunday morning public affairs program. Previously, Welker was co-anchor of “Weekend TODAY” and NBC News Chief White House Correspondent, where her political reporting appeared across all NBC News and MSNBC platforms. Welker began covering the White House for NBC News during the Obama administration. Subsequently, she covered Trump's presidency and the 2020 presidential race, and the network’s coverage of the Biden administration.  Kristen Welker is an American journalist known for her work with NBC. In 2011, she became a White House correspondent for the network. His reporting appears on all NBC News platforms, including “NBC Nightly News”, “Today”, “Meet the Press”, MSNBC and NBCNews.com. \t\t\n\nDid Kristen Welker's family visit the White House during Obama's presidency?\t\t\nIn 2012, Welker and her family celebrated Christmas at the White House with the Obamas. Though Kristen Welker’s party registration is not listed today, she was a registered Democrat in Washington, DC, in 2012 and in Rhode Island in 2004. Throughout Welker’s tenure as a White House correspondent, she has earned a reputation for a scathing style of questioning.  The people know! How’s Steve Scully doing?” Trump tweeted along with a retweet from son Donald Trump Jr., linking Welker and her family to prominent Democrats. Welker’s fami